{
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "travel_decline_risk_flag",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.15,
      "source_groundedness": 0.2,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly targets the query (decline risk on travel), but is a constant 0 across all 500 rows, so it provides zero discriminative leverage. The rows shown are hardware/cloud assets, not travel expenses, and nothing in the source supports a travel-decline determination; the flag is uniformly 0 by default rather than a grounded reading. Near-constant and effectively ungrounded."
    },
    {
      "name": "missing_source_id_indicator",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.35,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A data-completeness flag derived directly from presence/absence of source_id, which is verifiable. It has real variance (354/146). However it is only weakly connected to reducing declined travel expenses and largely restates an existing column's null-status, so analytical leverage for THIS query is limited."
    },
    {
      "name": "unprocessed_duration_days",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.1,
      "source_groundedness": 0.3,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Constant -1 across all 500 rows, providing no analytical signal. The sentinel presumably means 'processed' or 'uncomputable', but rows with valid processed_date still show -1, so it neither reflects the source nor discriminates. Near-constant and poorly grounded."
    },
    {
      "name": "amount_quartile",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.6,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Cleanly derived from the existing amount column with a well-balanced distribution (roughly 125 per quartile), giving a genuine axis to group/compare spend magnitude. Grounded in a real numeric field. Usefulness for the specific decline-reduction query is moderate since it is a generic transform of an existing column, but it does add binning leverage."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.32,
  "source_groundedness": 0.55,
  "rationale": "Two of four columns are near-constant (travel_decline_risk_flag all 0, unprocessed_duration_days all -1) and contribute no analytical leverage while also being poorly grounded. amount_quartile is a sound, grounded binning that offers real grouping value, and missing_source_id_indicator is well-grounded but only tangentially useful for the travel-decline question. Overall the set is weak on usefulness and mixed on groundedness."
}

